(A format string is appended to a buffer part by part, in place, so the
 second hole reads the buffer after the first hole's text has been added.
 Both appends grow the buffer.)
To 'merge' of a buffer called first and a buffer called second.
    append "{second}{second}" to first.
    Print "first {first's size} second {second's size}".

a buffer called hold is "abc".
For each number from 1 to 1000, append "abcdefgh" to hold.
Print "hold {hold's size}".
'merge' of hold and hold.
Print "hold {hold's size}".
